<title>BRAZIL: Soy shipping conditions at Brazil Paranagua/Santos.</title>
<headline>Soy shipping conditions at Brazil Paranagua/Santos.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian ports of</p>
<p>Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for</p>
<p>shipping soybeans and soyproducts.</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: Mariner A loading 54,359 soybeans, Ilenao loading 51,500 tonnes soymeal Waiting to dock: six vessels to load soymeal, two to load soybeans, one to load soybeans/meal Road: 253 trucks carrying soybeans arrived on August 14, 282 trucks with soymeal and 38 trucks with vegetable oils including</p>
<p>soyoil Loaded (August 14): 3,747 tonnes soybeans, 22,109 tonnes soymeal</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available</p>
<p>SANTOS</p>
<p>Vessels: Maria Diamanto loading 10,450 tonnes soymeal at public terminal, Orleta Lwowskie loading 57,500 tonnes soymeal at Cargill terminal</p>
<p>Waiting to dock: one vessel to load soymeal (awaiting arrival</p>
<p>of soymeal in port), three ships to load soybeans (two awaiting</p>
<p>soybeans)</p>
<p>Road (August 14): 34 trucks unloaded 896 tonnes soybeans</p>
<p>Rail (August 14): 96 wagons unloaded 5,386 tonnes soybeans</p>
<p>Loaded (August 14): nothing</p>
<p>Stocks: 35,438 tonnes soybeans, 14,779 tonnes soymeal</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
